Subject: [PATCH 334/335] Meridian: the Workbench's Claude Code and Codex tabs
 run the newest copy

With an old Claude Code (2.0.14) in /usr/local/bin first on the PATH and
the current one (2.1.332) in ~/.local/bin, the Workbench's Claude Code
tab started the old one: it looked the CLI up on the PATH, while Ask,
Improve, sign-in and Connect already took the newest copy.

The Workbench now starts every agent CLI by the full path of its newest
copy (ai::FindNewestCli): the agent tabs, Resume, a session reopened
after a restart and Remote Control, and what the launcher shows. A shell
tab gets the newest Claude Code's and Codex's folders first on its PATH
when the PATH would find an older copy first, and zsh puts them in front
again after its startup files and macOS's path_helper (.zlogin), so
`claude` typed there is the current one too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
